1
00:00:02,200 --> 00:00:04,100
Look around you.

2
00:00:04,667 --> 00:00:07,200
Before breakfast is even over,

3
00:00:07,200 --> 00:00:10,000
technology is already working for you.

4
00:00:10,600 --> 00:00:11,933
A phone lights up.

5
00:00:11,933 --> 00:00:14,467
A map finds the fastest way to school.

6
00:00:14,467 --> 00:00:15,767
A song starts playing,

7
00:00:15,767 --> 00:00:17,100
picked just for you.

8
00:00:17,767 --> 00:00:19,333
None of it is magic.

9
00:00:19,333 --> 00:00:21,633
Every tap, every screen,

10
00:00:21,633 --> 00:00:23,400
every message was planned,

11
00:00:23,400 --> 00:00:25,900
designed, and built by people who learned to

12
00:00:25,900 --> 00:00:26,800
code.

13
00:00:28,400 --> 00:00:30,367
Welcome to the world of coding.

14
00:00:30,833 --> 00:00:33,500
Today, we're going on a journey from ideas

15
00:00:33,500 --> 00:00:35,067
to real products.

16
00:00:37,267 --> 00:00:38,933
Let's start with something you might use

17
00:00:38,933 --> 00:00:40,000
every week.

18
00:00:40,367 --> 00:00:42,867
You're hungry, so you open a food delivery

19
00:00:42,867 --> 00:00:43,767
app.

20
00:00:44,033 --> 00:00:45,867
You scroll through the restaurants,

21
00:00:45,867 --> 00:00:47,500
choose your favorite meal,

22
00:00:47,500 --> 00:00:49,367
and tap, place order.

23
00:00:49,933 --> 00:00:52,433
Instantly, the kitchen receives it,

24
00:00:52,433 --> 00:00:54,100
a rider is on the way,

25
00:00:54,100 --> 00:00:56,233
and you can watch them move across a live

26
00:00:56,233 --> 00:00:58,167
map, right to your door.

27
00:00:58,867 --> 00:01:01,200
Every screen, every button,

28
00:01:01,200 --> 00:01:03,200
even that little moving map.

29
00:01:03,200 --> 00:01:04,433
Someone coded it.

30
00:01:06,000 --> 00:01:07,900
Now think about school.

31
00:01:08,267 --> 00:01:09,633
At the end of the term,

32
00:01:09,633 --> 00:01:11,533
parents don't have to wait for a paper

33
00:01:11,533 --> 00:01:12,433
report.

34
00:01:12,933 --> 00:01:14,600
They open the school portal,

35
00:01:14,600 --> 00:01:17,067
sign in securely, and there it is.

36
00:01:17,067 --> 00:01:19,200
Every subject, every grade,

37
00:01:19,200 --> 00:01:20,967
and a message from the teacher.

38
00:01:21,633 --> 00:01:23,500
That portal is a website.

39
00:01:23,500 --> 00:01:24,733
And somebody built it,

40
00:01:24,733 --> 00:01:25,900
line by line.

41
00:01:27,400 --> 00:01:30,033
Once you notice it, you see it everywhere.

42
00:01:30,500 --> 00:01:32,900
The online store where you add new sneakers

43
00:01:32,900 --> 00:01:33,967
to your cart.

44
00:01:34,367 --> 00:01:36,800
The transport app that tells you your bus is

45
00:01:36,800 --> 00:01:38,233
three minutes away.

46
00:01:38,833 --> 00:01:41,233
Every one of them started as an idea,

47
00:01:41,233 --> 00:01:43,300
and every one of them runs on code.

48
00:01:44,800 --> 00:01:46,700
So, what actually is coding?

49
00:01:47,267 --> 00:01:49,133
Coding is writing instructions for a

50
00:01:49,133 --> 00:01:50,100
computer.

51
00:01:50,667 --> 00:01:53,067
Computers are incredibly fast,

52
00:01:53,067 --> 00:01:55,000
but they can't guess what you mean.

53
00:01:55,000 --> 00:01:56,800
They do exactly what you tell them,

54
00:01:56,800 --> 00:01:58,933
step by step, in order.

55
00:01:59,533 --> 00:02:01,533
So a coder takes an idea,

56
00:02:01,533 --> 00:02:03,767
like, when someone taps add,

57
00:02:03,767 --> 00:02:05,367
put the meal in the cart,

58
00:02:05,367 --> 00:02:07,500
and turns it into clear steps the computer

59
00:02:07,500 --> 00:02:08,500
can follow.

60
00:02:09,000 --> 00:02:11,933
Write the steps, and the product responds.

61
00:02:13,400 --> 00:02:15,233
And here's the exciting part.

62
00:02:15,233 --> 00:02:16,900
Once you can give instructions,

63
00:02:16,900 --> 00:02:18,833
you can build almost anything.

64
00:02:19,433 --> 00:02:21,767
Websites. Mobile apps.

65
00:02:21,767 --> 00:02:23,033
School systems.

66
00:02:23,033 --> 00:02:25,967
Games. Digital tools that help people.

67
00:02:25,967 --> 00:02:28,600
Even the systems that run whole businesses.

68
00:02:29,167 --> 00:02:31,400
And most of what you see on a screen starts

69
00:02:31,400 --> 00:02:33,900
with the same three building blocks.

70
00:02:35,367 --> 00:02:37,367
The first is HTML.

71
00:02:37,367 --> 00:02:39,467
HTML is the structure.

72
00:02:39,933 --> 00:02:42,333
Think of it like the frame of a house.

73
00:02:42,333 --> 00:02:44,300
It decides what's on the page.

74
00:02:44,300 --> 00:02:45,133
A heading.

75
00:02:45,133 --> 00:02:46,067
A picture.

76
00:02:46,067 --> 00:02:47,200
Some text.

77
00:02:47,200 --> 00:02:48,100
A button.

78
00:02:48,533 --> 00:02:51,533
Without HTML, there's nothing there at all.

79
00:02:52,900 --> 00:02:55,067
The second is CSS.

80
00:02:55,067 --> 00:02:57,300
CSS is the appearance.

81
00:02:57,767 --> 00:02:59,833
It's the paint and the design.

82
00:02:59,833 --> 00:03:01,700
The colors, the fonts,

83
00:03:01,700 --> 00:03:04,200
the spacing, the rounded corners.

84
00:03:04,667 --> 00:03:07,800
CSS turns a plain page into something that

85
00:03:07,800 --> 00:03:10,467
looks beautiful and feels professional.

86
00:03:11,867 --> 00:03:13,900
The third is JavaScript.

87
00:03:13,900 --> 00:03:15,900
JavaScript is the behavior.

88
00:03:16,400 --> 00:03:17,900
It makes things happen.

89
00:03:17,900 --> 00:03:19,100
When you tap a button,

90
00:03:19,100 --> 00:03:21,600
JavaScript decides what comes next.

91
00:03:22,067 --> 00:03:23,267
It counts.

92
00:03:23,267 --> 00:03:24,267
It checks.

93
00:03:24,267 --> 00:03:25,500
It responds.

94
00:03:25,500 --> 00:03:27,300
It's the electricity that switches the

95
00:03:27,300 --> 00:03:28,333
lights on.

96
00:03:29,733 --> 00:03:31,633
Now put them together.

97
00:03:32,100 --> 00:03:34,400
HTML gives it structure.

98
00:03:34,400 --> 00:03:36,267
CSS makes it look great.

99
00:03:36,267 --> 00:03:38,233
JavaScript brings it to life.

100
00:03:38,833 --> 00:03:40,133
Three layers.

101
00:03:40,133 --> 00:03:41,467
One real product.

102
00:03:41,467 --> 00:03:42,733
That's how the food app,

103
00:03:42,733 --> 00:03:45,367
the school portal, and almost every website

104
00:03:45,367 --> 00:03:46,733
you love are made.

105
00:03:48,233 --> 00:03:50,733
And today, creators have a powerful new

106
00:03:50,733 --> 00:03:52,467
helper. AI.

107
00:03:53,067 --> 00:03:55,067
Tools like Claude can explain a line of

108
00:03:55,067 --> 00:03:57,567
code, help you track down a bug,

109
00:03:57,567 --> 00:04:00,200
or suggest a better idea when you're stuck.

110
00:04:00,767 --> 00:04:03,533
But AI is a tool, not the builder.

111
00:04:03,533 --> 00:04:04,967
You bring the ideas.

112
00:04:04,967 --> 00:04:06,467
You make the decisions.

113
00:04:06,467 --> 00:04:08,433
And you understand what you create.

114
00:04:08,833 --> 00:04:11,000
AI just helps you get there faster.

115
00:04:12,567 --> 00:04:14,300
So here's the big idea.

116
00:04:14,300 --> 00:04:16,567
Every app you use was built by people who

117
00:04:16,567 --> 00:04:19,133
started exactly where you are right now.

118
00:04:19,733 --> 00:04:20,967
They had an idea.

119
00:04:20,967 --> 00:04:22,800
They learned the building blocks.

120
00:04:22,800 --> 00:04:24,000
And they kept going.

121
00:04:24,767 --> 00:04:27,033
Welcome to Paisley Tech Studio.

122
00:04:27,033 --> 00:04:28,700
This is where you stop just using

123
00:04:28,700 --> 00:04:31,167
technology, and start creating it.

124
00:04:31,867 --> 00:04:34,467
Let's build something amazing, together.
